From d7ead97925630abd5b03cdbed9084d1d4d43b293 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alexvnesta <alex.v.nesta@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:05:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Generator: fair scheduling between prompt ingestion and
 generation

New Generator arguments fair_gen_rounds (default 1) and fair_chunk_size (default None). While the active set
mixes jobs that still ingest a prompt with jobs that are already generating, iterate() can run fair_gen_rounds
generation steps per prefill chunk and shrink the prefill chunk to fair_chunk_size (a multiple of the 256-token
page), so streaming jobs keep emitting tokens while a long prompt is ingested. Job.prefill takes the chunk
size. With the defaults the scheduler behaves as before (one round, full chunk).

No upstream counterpart (same argument names as open upstream PR #448).

Port of public-repo engine patch 0006 onto upstream dev 0f685aa9fd (P16), by hand (not a 3-way merge).
job.py: same hunk. generator.py: dev restructured the generation block into draft -> iterate_hybrid_gen ->
iterate_gen; the whole block, including the hybrid substitution, now runs inside the gen_rounds loop, so each
extra fair round drafts, substitutes and verifies like a normal round (as the deployed hybrid wrapper did, which
replaced the drafting method itself). Two compatibility changes against the deployed patch, both on the default
path only: the fair settings are also class attributes (a generator built without __init__ schedules as
before), and when no fair chunk applies iterate() calls Job.prefill(results) with one argument, exactly as
upstream does, so callers and hooks that only know prefill(results) keep working.

Test: tests/generator/test_fair_scheduling.py (CPU).
---
 exllamav3/generator/generator.py        | 103 ++++++++---
 exllamav3/generator/job.py              |  11 +-
 tests/generator/test_fair_scheduling.py | 222 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 313 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/generator/test_fair_scheduling.py

